    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30805" root="عنق" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَنِّقَاتٌ</span></b> , applied to mountains (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِبَال</span>) accord.
to the copies of the K, [and thus in the O,] but
correctly <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِبَال</span>, with the unpointed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ح</span>, (TA,)
[i. e. elongated and elevated tracts of sand,] signifies <i>Long.</i> (O, K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُعَنَّقَةُ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُعَنِّقَةُ</span> as signifying <i>Hectic fever</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُمَّى الدِّقِّ</span>) is
post-classical. (TA.)

